@startuml
title Scope hierarchy semantics: entry, regions, history, completion
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #ECF5FC
  BorderColor #477B9B
  StartColor #2F7C5A
  EndColor #7D478F
  ArrowColor #496174
}

state "Root scope" as Root #E9F5EA {
  state "Intake" as Intake #DCEEFF
  [*] --> Intake
  Intake --> ReviewScope : completed

  state "ReviewScope (parallel)" as ReviewScope #FFF0D9 {
    state "Draft answer" as DraftAnswer #DCEEFF
    state "Critique loop" as CritiqueLoop #DCEEFF
    [*] --> DraftAnswer
    DraftAnswer --> CritiqueLoop : completed
    CritiqueLoop --> CritiqueLoop : needsWork\n[<latex>\kappa < b</latex>] / <latex>\kappa{+}{+}</latex>
    [H] --> DraftAnswer
    --
    state "Safety screen" as SafetyScreen #E7DCF5
    state "Escalate" as Escalate #E7DCF5
    [*] --> SafetyScreen
    SafetyScreen --> Escalate : flagged
  }
  ReviewScope : entry / run entry activities (sequential observed effects)
  ReviewScope : exit / snapshot history, then run exit activities

  state "Approval" as Approval #FFE0C8
  ReviewScope --> Approval : completed (all-join of regions)
  Approval --> ReviewScope[H*] : rejected / deep re-entry\nrestores the remembered configuration
  state "Publish" as Publish #D9EFDF
  Approval --> Publish : approved
  Publish --> [*]
}
Root --> [*]

note right of ReviewScope #EAF7EE
Regions are a modeling view. The kernel realizes
orthogonality as multiple tokens in one flat scope
(ScopeInstance, runtime.rs:1499-1514); completion is
token-count exhaustion, not per-region final states.
History captures the key set of the active configuration
at completion: <latex>h(s) = \mathrm{keys}(\mathit{act}_{\sigma})</latex>.
end note
note left of Approval #FFF3C9
After the first completion of a history-declaring
scope, plain re-entry also restores the remembered
configuration (no history node required, no mode
filter): the initial pseudostate becomes a default
history pseudostate.
end note
@enduml
